=20

Dear Administrative Court,

Further to your email of 28 November, I now resubmit the fully ACO-complian=
t consolidated bundle for my Judicial Review claim (N461) together with the =
urgent application for expedition (N463).

The bundle is now presented as a single paginated PDF including:
Full Index
N461 Claim Form + continuation sheets
N463 Urgent Application + continuation sheets
Detailed Grounds
Witness Statement (WS1)
Exhibits A=E2=80=93D
Medical evidence (including the signed report from Dr Bruce Hayse)
Draft Order
Authorities
=20

This addresses every point raised in your guidance, including the requireme=
nt for a single document, pagination, and inclusion of both applications wit=
hin one bundle.

=20

Medical urgency =E2=80=94 Equality Act and PSED duties engaged

=20

As the Court is aware, I am a vulnerable litigant with Autism Spectrum Cond=
ition and PTSD.

My treating physician, Dr Bruce Hayse, has confirmed in his signed medical =
report that:
I am at acute medical and psychiatric risk,
delays in the Court process are materially worsening my condition, and
urgent judicial action is required to prevent clinical deterioration.
=20

I was hospitalised this weekend with acute abdominal pain directly linked t=
o stress.

The Court owes duties under:
Equality Act 2010 (ss.20=E2=80=9321),
Public Sector Equality Duty (s.149), and
the Overriding Objective
=20

to ensure that my applications are processed promptly and safely.

Urgent Request

Given that:
the N463 application has been pending since 25 November,
the Defendants were properly served,
and the complete ACO-compliant bundle is now filed,
=20

I respectfully request that the Court:
Confirm sealing of the claim today,
Issue a case reference number, and
Place the N463 before a judge immediately for urgent consideration.
=20

Any further delay would present a significant, medically-documented safegua=
rding risk.

=20

I would be grateful for confirmation as soon as possible.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

=20

CC:

Administrative Court Office =E2=80=94 Case Progression

Administrative Court Office =E2=80=94 List Office

