Dear Administrative Court General Office,

=20

I write further to my urgent filing today of an ACO-compliant N461 Judicial=
 Review bundle in Zahmoul v Ministry of Justice & HMCTS, and to my email to =
Case Progression requesting a case reference number.

=20

I have been informed that no assistance can be provided by Case Progression=
 until a case reference number has been allocated, and that I must therefore=
 contact the General Office.

=20

Accordingly, I respectfully request that:
A case reference number for my N461 Judicial Review claim be allocated as a=
 matter of urgency; and
Confirmation be provided that my N461 bundle (sent today under the subject =
line =E2=80=9CN461 Urgent Bundle =E2=80=93 Zahmoul v MoJ & HMCTS=E2=80=9D) has been received a=
nd accepted for issue.
=20

This matter is medically urgent. My treating physician, Dr Bruce Hayse, has=
 provided a signed report confirming that I am in a clinically fragile psych=
iatric state and that delay in the Court process creates a significant safeg=
uarding risk. I am a disabled litigant (Autism and PTSD), and the Court=E2=80=99s =
duties under the Equality Act 2010 and the Public Sector Equality Duty (s.14=
9) are therefore engaged.

=20

I am acting as a litigant in person and do not have the financial means to =
obtain legal representation. I have done everything I can to comply with the=
 Administrative Court=E2=80=99s requirements and to provide a single, court-ready =
N461 bundle.

=20

For these reasons, I would be very grateful if a case reference number coul=
d be issued today, and if my claim could then be progressed to case progress=
ion for urgent consideration alongside my N463 application.

=20

Yours faithfully,

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

Email: Nadia@rosekross.com

